==English==

===Etymology===
First use appears c. 1911. See cite below.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-bum's rush.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally|North America|slang|idiomatic}} The [[forcible]] [[ejection]] of someone, such as a [[bum]] or a [[hobo]], from an [[establishment]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1911|month=March|work=Ambition: A Journal of Inspiration to Self Help|title=Blowing the Crowd|author=Wm. Hamilton Osborne|volume=9|number=8|passage="I didnt' think you fellows'd put the '''bum's rush''' onto me," he complained, "I ain't no bum."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948| title=Daily Labor Report - Issues 181-210 |author=| page=326| passage=It seems that the board appointed to look into alleged shortcomings of leftish Council leaders didn't like the "observers" who were brought along and decided to give them the '''bum's rush'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1982|author={{w|Paul Radley}}|title=My Blue-Checker Corker and Me|publisher=Fontana/Collins|location=Sydney|page=96|text=At that point Duck got the '''bum’s rush''' from the organising Miss Bowen[.]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Thinner This Year: A Younger Next Year Book|author=Chris Crowley; Jennifer Sacheck | page=| passage=But suddenly he has a lucid interval . . . senses exactly what is going on. And he gives me this furious look. Astonishes me by saying, with all the old force, in his old, frightening growl: “This is a '''bum's rush'''!”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Bees Make the Best Pets|author=Jack Mingo | page=81| passage=Early last September, some fellow beekeepers reported that the females in their bee colonies had already given the '''bum's rush''' to the males, the drones, kicking them out in the cold.}}

